            {
                "entry_id": "b5b269f9-f8eb-3cbd-8dd8-4d5028c6a7c5",
                "word": "controversiste",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2d89336c-36fe-4844-8bf4-6728c0219b5b",
                        "entry_id": "b5b269f9-f8eb-3cbd-8dd8-4d5028c6a7c5",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "controversistes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a09d341-497e-3444-a56e-39c2fa667712",
                        "entry_id": "b5b269f9-f8eb-3cbd-8dd8-4d5028c6a7c5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Celui qui traite de sujets de controverse religieuse."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1251a4c4-695b-44b2-8e2f-088a7f668bd8",
                                "sense_id": "5a09d341-497e-3444-a56e-39c2fa667712",
                                "text": "On n’a recours aux invectives que quand on manque de preuves. Entre deux controversistes, il y a cent à parier contre un, que celui qui aura tort se fâchera."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3dbd192a-6b82-4dac-943b-69e151feabdc",
                                "sense_id": "5a09d341-497e-3444-a56e-39c2fa667712",
                                "text": "Il est vrai, […], que le juifs, plus versés que les prêtres chrétiens dans la connaissance des Écritures, étaient de redoutables controversistes, à ce point que Saint Louis manifesta sa répugnance pour les discussions entre les juifs et les chrétiens insuffisamment instruits : […]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a970638e-478b-4357-87eb-036286aac845",
                                "sense_id": "5a09d341-497e-3444-a56e-39c2fa667712",
                                "text": "Je n’ai pas besoin, remarquez bien, de me poser ici en controversiste, de prouver qu’il y a contradiction entre la science et la révélation […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a23597fb-6c4f-476f-8ceb-5f7db2f7090c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b5b269f9-f8eb-3cbd-8dd8-4d5028c6a7c5",
                        "source_sense_id": "5a09d341-497e-3444-a56e-39c2fa667712",
                        "target_lang_word": "controversialist",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "controversialist",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                        "entry_id": "ae4b133d-6e74-3a93-868b-ea973ef7f6b0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who regularly engages in public controversies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "745d9aa9-10e6-4061-a1d1-eae799666291",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "Richard Dawkins has become a leading controversialist in a few areas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46c29f89-9f58-454a-b0bf-1a2ff83861da",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "His indefatigable adversary, who is the perfect model of an agile controversialist, had attacked him as a magniloquent Thraso, on account of his Pansophical promises."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2abd8de6-e338-47b1-a834-1fa19d9d9263",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "Does this explain the sensational character of some of his public pronouncements? A controversialist might drive through some of the later chapters with a coach and four without encountering serious impediments; but sono ben trovati, and he is a hold man who would presume to pass final judgment upon the contemporary phase of Italy’s history."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9a46025b-b196-40d2-b312-9d39ff22363b",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "He was not a drunkard, not a chronic bankrupt. For the rest, Mr. Woodward depicts [Thomas] Paine as a highminded controversialist, persecuted by reactionaries on both sides of the Atlantic for no more than liberal political views."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "47b8a515-2aa1-4116-8903-21a250ef3348",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "In the early 1700s [Jonathan] Swift spent much of his time in London, where he wormed his way into the company of coffee-house wits and politicians, and, beginning to publish political tracts, won a reputation as a controversialist."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad529586-bdd9-400f-b6e6-366bdd0638ca",
                                                "sense_id": "0d25fde0-6f36-306f-b7aa-cf9c1c7aa55b",
                                                "text": "This was to have been the final date of the rightwing controversialist’s charmingly named Dangerous Faggot Tour of US campuses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": []
            }
